# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  KSRM deployment — the exam module of the KSRM website
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Copy to `.env.production` before `npm run build`.
#
#  With these set the product presents itself as KSRM's own examination module:
#  no institution sign-up, no third-party platform name, KSRM branding on the
#  screens candidates and staff actually see.

# Serve the app under a subpath of the main site. Every asset URL and the
# router's basename derive from this, so it is the single switch that moves the
# whole app. Leave unset to serve from a domain root instead.
VITE_BASE_PATH=/online/

# Where the Spring Boot API is reachable. Must be https in production, or the
# browser blocks every request from an https page as mixed content.
# Under the subpath deployment nginx proxies this to the backend on :8080.
VITE_API_URL=https://ksrmce.ac.in/online/api

# Pins this build to KSRM. Candidates then type only their hall ticket and name,
# and the sign-in page shows the KSRM name and logo.
# Use the code returned when the KSRM admin account was created.
VITE_INSTITUTION_CODE=ksrm-college

# No self-registration. The staff accounts are created by KSRM, not signed up
# for. The server enforces this as well — see app.registration.enabled.
VITE_ALLOW_REGISTRATION=false

# What the product calls itself where no college name applies.
VITE_PLATFORM_NAME="KSRM Examinations"

# The sign-in screens open on the college crest drawing itself — the same
# 4-second clip the main KSRM site opens with, taken unchanged from that site's
# frontend/public/ksrm-logo.webm. The files live in public/branding, so
# replacing logo-intro.webm and logo.webp re-dresses the screen for another
# institution; these two variables exist for a deployment that would rather
# serve them from somewhere else.
#
# The clip is WebM carrying an alpha channel, which is what lets the crest sit
# on the panel without a box around it. Do not re-encode it casually: ffmpeg
# does not carry a WebM alpha channel through a transcode, and the result looks
# right on a dark background while being a black square on any other. Safari
# cannot play WebM alpha at all, so logo.webp is shown there instead — which is
# why that still must be the finished crest and must itself be transparent.
#
# It is 418 kB, fetched by every machine in the hall within the same minute.
# That is the college's own asset and worth the bytes, but anything larger
# would be felt as a slow sign-in by five thousand people at once.
# VITE_SIGNIN_LOGO_INTRO=/branding/logo-intro.webm
# VITE_SIGNIN_LOGO=/branding/logo.webp

# Note: values containing spaces are quoted. This file is often loaded with
# `set -a; . ./.env.production; set +a`, and bash splits an unquoted value on
# the space — which once left the platform name empty in a production build,
# with only a "command not found" scrolling past to say so.
